  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1547483238-f400e65ccd56?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Drive Gauge is the most important resource in SF6—never deplete it fully (Burnout state removes Drive Parry and Drive Impact access, making you highly susceptible to chip damage and corner pressure).",
      "Drive Impact (DI) can absorb 2 hits and stagger the opponent—always have a DI answer ready when you are cornered, as DI is the fastest way to reset corner position. DI on reaction to opponent DI is the most reliable counter.",
      "Overdrive (OD) special moves cost 2 Drive stocks and are integral to high-damage combos—budget 3 Drive stocks minimum before attempting any combo that requires an OD extension. Running OD combos with insufficient gauge causes Burnout mid-combo.",
      "The Parry timing for Drive Parry is the same 1-frame window as classic SF3 parry but with a visual cue (blue flash)—holding Parry in neutral absorbs attacks but drains Drive Gauge; use it only against confirmed attacks, not speculatively.",
      "Modern Control assists (auto combo button) allow easier special moves but reduce damage output by 10–20%—Classic Control is required for highest-level play but Modern provides a legitimate path to Diamond rank with lower technical demands."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "ドライブゲージはSF6で最も重要なリソース。完全に消費するとバーンアウト状態になりドライブパリィとドライブインパクトが使えなくなり、チップダメージと画面端プレッシャーに弱くなる。",
      "ドライブインパクト（DI）は2ヒット吸収して相手をよろけさせる。コーナーに追い詰められた時は常にDIの答えを準備する。相手DIへのDIで返すのが最も信頼できるカウンター。",
      "OD（オーバードライブ）必殺技はドライブストック2つを消費し、高ダメージコンボに不可欠。OD延長が必要なコンボを試みる前に最低3ドライブストックを確保する。ゲージ不足でODコンボを始めると中断時にバーンアウトになる。",
      "ドライブパリィのタイミングはSF3のクラシックパリィと同じ1フレームウィンドウだが視覚的なキュー（青い閃光）がある。ニュートラルでパリィを保持すると攻撃を吸収するがドライブゲージを消費する。確認できた攻撃にのみ使用し、憶測で使わない。",
      "モダンコントロール（オートコンボボタン）は簡単な必殺技を可能にするがダメージが10〜20%低下する。最高レベルのプレイにはクラシックコントロールが必要だが、モダンはダイヤモンドランクまで技術的要求が低い正規のルートを提供する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Character Fundamentals and Drive Gauge Basics",
        "body": "Choose a character with a straightforward gameplan for your first 100 hours: Ryu, Ken, Luke, or Kimberly each have clear win conditions and well-documented beginner combo routes. In the first 20 hours, focus exclusively on two mechanics: Drive Impact timing (confirming a hit on blocked DI) and anti-air responses (your character's primary anti-air move—usually Heavy Punch or Dragon Punch variant). Most losses at beginner rank come from no anti-air response and inability to punish blocked DI, not from combo execution."
      },
      {
        "title": "World Tour Mode for Fundamentals",
        "body": "World Tour (single player story mode) is the best space to practice Drive Gauge management under pressure—the mode features real-time combat with Drive Gauge mechanics identical to VS mode. Use World Tour to learn Drive Parry timing on repeated incoming moves (NPC enemies repeat attack patterns) and to practice OD combo routes without opponent pressure. Complete World Tour up to Master Rashid to unlock the Rashid character move set as a non-DLC option."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Corner Carry and Mix-up Theory",
        "body": "Corner position is a significant advantage in SF6—drive rush (forward dash from Drive) extends combo corner carry by 30–50% compared to raw combos. The primary corner mix-up that most characters use: meaty normal → opponent wakes up → low sweep (true low) vs. throw (true mid) vs. overhead (optional, character-specific). Understanding which of these three options your character has and which two-option mix they can execute consistently determines your floor in ranked play."
      },
      {
        "title": "SA (Super Art) Integration",
        "body": "Each character has 3 Super Arts (SA1, SA2, SA3) that cost varying Super Gauge amounts. SA3 (maximum gauge) provides the highest damage but fewest activations per round—for most characters, two SA2 activations per round outperform one SA3 in total round damage output. Learn your character's SA combo integration: which normal attacks link into SA, whether SA is combo-convertible after Drive Rush, and the safe-on-block windows for SA1 feints."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Master Rank Neutral Game",
        "body": "At Master rank, neutral game centres on walk-speed whiff punishment and footsie conditioning. The footsie conditioning loop: throw your dominant mid-range poke 3 times to condition the opponent to step back, then once they step back, Drive Rush through their retreat for a full combo. This sequence is difficult to defend once established and forms the backbone of high-level neutral. Anti-Drive Rush options (DI, neutral Heavy Punch) must also be learned simultaneously as opponents will attempt the same gameplan against you."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Wasting Drive stocks on blocked Drive Rush—Drive Rush costs 1.5 Drive stocks and can be interrupted on block; only Drive Rush into safe normals (at least -2 on block or better) to avoid losing stocks to reversals.",
      "Using SA as a reversal without confirming the opponent's advantage—SA1 has invincibility frames but SA3 does not on most characters; confirm whether your SA has invincibility before using it as a wake-up reversal.",
      "Neglecting the Perfect Parry window (2 frames after Drive Parry activation)—Perfect Parry provides a free punish window; landing one against an unsafe move is a full combo conversion.",
      "Not labbing punish combos for the 15 most common unsafe moves—every character has reliable unsafe moves at intermediate play; knowing your 2-3 most damaging punish routes for each of those moves significantly increases win rate.",
      "Playing Drive Rush on opponent's wake-up without a mix-up plan—Drive Rush with no mix-up is easily punished by reversal SA; commit Drive Rush approach only when you have a meaty setup or throw trap prepared."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "ガードされたドライブラッシュにドライブストックを浪費する。ドライブラッシュはストック1.5つを消費し、ガードされると割り込まれる可能性がある。リバーサルでストックを失わないよう、ガード時安全な（-2以上）通常技にのみドライブラッシュする。",
      "相手の有利状況を確認せずにSAをリバーサルとして使う。SA1は無敵フレームを持つが、ほとんどのキャラクターのSA3には無敵がない。SAを起き上がりリバーサルとして使う前に、SAに無敵があるかどうかを確認する。",
      "パーフェクトパリィのウィンドウ（ドライブパリィ発動後2フレーム）を無視する。パーフェクトパリィは無料の確定反撃ウィンドウを提供する。安全でない技に対してパーフェクトパリィを当てると全コンボに変換できる。",
      "最も一般的な15の安全でない技に対する確定反撃コンボを研究しない。全てのキャラクターは中級プレイで信頼できる安全でない技を持つ。それぞれに対する2〜3の最もダメージの高い確定反撃ルートを知ることで勝率が大きく向上する。",
      "ミックスアップ計画なしで相手の起き上がりにドライブラッシュをかける。ミックスアップなしのドライブラッシュはリバーサルSAで簡単に対処される。生攻めドライブラッシュはミートセットアップかスロートラップを準備した時のみ行う。"
